%% alt: Session-based authentication sequence — when a user logs in with id/pw, the server creates a session, stores it, and sends the session ID back as a cookie. On every subsequent request, the browser automatically attaches the cookie, and the server looks up the session store by session ID to identify the user
sequenceDiagram
    participant B as Browser
    participant S as Server
    participant D as Session store<br/>(Memory · DB · Redis)
    B->>S: 1. Login (id / pw)
    S->>S: 2. Verify id/pw
    S->>D: Save session<br/>abc123 → Kim Chulsoo
    S-->>B: Send session ID(abc123) as cookie
    Note over B: Browser stores cookie
    B->>S: 3. Subsequent request (cookie abc123 auto-attached)
    S->>D: 4. Look up abc123
    D-->>S: Kim Chulsoo
    S-->>B: Response (identifies user and processes)
